# Per-user topic ACL for the Mosquitto broker.
# Source: mosquitto.org/documentation/plugins/acl-file/
#
# Default-deny: an authenticated user with no matching "user" block below
# gets NO access at all. A bare "topic" line outside a "user" block would
# apply only to anonymous clients, and allow_anonymous is false in
# deploy/mosquitto.conf, so no such line is written here.

user poller
topic readwrite #

user wsreader
topic read lan/#

# Admin dashboard login (`?admin=1`). Its only write grant is the admin command
# topic. Admin topics live outside `lan/`, so wsreader never sees them. `read
# lan/#` is granted so the admin page can show the normal dashboard on one
# connection (user-confirmed 2026-10-02, amending the original grant design);
# wsadmin still cannot write anywhere under `lan/`.
user wsadmin
topic read lan/#
topic read admin/ack
topic read admin/faked
topic write admin/cmd
